● Step-by-step: Python 3.11 venv for PaddleOCR

  Step 1 — Download Python 3.11

  Go to: https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3119/

  Scroll down to Files, download: Windows installer (64-bit)

  Run the installer:
  - Check "Add python.exe to PATH"
  - Click "Install Now"

  Don't uninstall Python 3.13 — they coexist fine.

  Step 2 — Verify Python 3.11 installed

  Open a new CMD or PowerShell and run:

  py -3.11 --version

  You should see Python 3.11.9. If py doesn't work, try:
  "C:\Users\User004\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python311\python.exe" --version

  Step 3 — Create a virtual environment

  In your project folder:

  cd C:\Users\User004\Desktop\soufian_data\new
  py -3.11 -m venv ocr_env

  This creates an ocr_env folder with a clean Python 3.11.

  Step 4 — Activate the venv

  ocr_env\Scripts\activate

  Your prompt should now show (ocr_env). Verify:
  python --version
  Should say Python 3.11.9.

  Step 5 — Install everything in the venv

  Run these in order:

  python -m pip install --upgrade pip
  python -m pip install jupyter notebook ipykernel
  python -m pip install paddlepaddle==3.0.0 -i https://www.paddlepaddle.org.cn/packages/stable/cpu/
  python -m pip install paddleocr
  pip install shapely scikit-image "protobuf>=3.20.0,<4.0"
  pip install opencv-python numpy matplotlib

  Step 6 — Register venv as a Jupyter kernel

  python -m ipykernel install --user --name=ocr_env --display-name "Python 3.11 (OCR)"

  Step 7 — Launch Jupyter and switch kernel

  jupyter notebook

  Open paddleocr_test.ipynb, then:
  - Click Kernel → Change kernel → Python 3.11 (OCR)
  - Re-run the cells

